    "result_text": "All 22 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature \u2014 on owner creation, the response (and subsequent GETs) reports the number of existing owners that already share the same first and last name, compared case-insensitively (excluding the owner being created).\n\nChanges, following the existing `customerCode` pattern for a computed-on-create, persisted field:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persistent `namesake_count` column mapping (`Integer namesakeCount`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` by name.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)` helper that counts existing owners with a case-insensitive first+last-name match (before the new owner is saved), and set it on the owner prior to `saveOwner`.\n\n4. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\nCp13 (`coreCountsNamesakes`) passes, and the full suite is green (22 tests, 0 failures).",
